                              FR (Files-Reverse)
               The nocTurne deSign /X Reverse File Lister V1.2

         (Users of V1.0-1.1 need only to read the 'Changes' section)

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 OVERVIEW
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
FR  allows  users  to view a file listing in its reverse order, ie the newer
descriptions  are  outputted  first.    It  should  be  of value to users of
relatively  competitive  boards,  where  the newest uploads of the day are a
priority.  This door works under AmiExpress 2.x-3.x and Sigma Express.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 INSTALLATION
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
This  program  is an XIM and should be installed as such.  Knowledge of door
installation is assumed.  Icons have been provided for 3.x owners.

The 'FR.x' info file has four options available.  If you want to disable the
dividers  between  each  filename,  simply  replace  the yes in the tooltype
"Dividers=YES" with a no.  If you want to disable the colors in the listing,
toggle  the  yes  in  "Colors=YES".  To disable the date-divider graphic, ie
what  appears  when  there  is  a  date  change  in  the listing, change the
"ShowNewDate"  tooltype.    If  you  are  using  a  nocTurne deSign Who Door
(noC-WHO), set "NocWhoCompat" to YES.

(All above options with the exception of "NocWhoCompat" may be overridden by
the user.  You are only setting the DEFAULTS for the user.)

If  you  would  like  a  different divider graphic than the default, (a blue
sequence  of  "======" ), you may design your own.  FR will utilize the text
in  the  file  "Doors:noC-FR/FR-Div.txt" if it exists.  Please keep the file
ONE  line  long,  with NO RETURN on the end.  You may use ansi colors in the
file.

If  you  want  a  different  date-divider graphic, edit/make a new text file
called  "Doors:noC-FR/FR-Date.txt".   The file should again be ONE line long
with  no tail return.  To denote where (if anyplace) the date should go, use
"@THEDATE".

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
 USAGE
----------------------------------------------------------------------------
After  typing  'FR'  without any arguments from the command line, files from
the  upload  directory  of  the  current  conference are displayed newest to
oldest.  (Please note: The door name 'FR' should never be altered).  Several
options  are available to the user.  Some of the fundamental usage arguments
are:


'FR ?' will bring up information on the program and its usage.

'FR  O'  will  run  the door with configurable parameters.  The user will be
prompted  for the date from which the listing should start and the directory
to  list.  If there is more than one directory, the user may select from the
alternatives.
     
'FR  E' will allow the user to configure FR to his own taste.  Configuration
data will go to the file "DOORS:noC-FR/fr-users.dat".
     

When  the listing is paused, the user may flag files, abort the listing, set
the  listing  to  nonstop  mode,  or continue.  CTRL-C aborts are supported.
Usage is very intuitive, I don't think any more detail is neccessary.

